  _landmarkId: el-hamra-sarayi
  _displayTitle: Alhambra Palace
  _shortDescription: The Alhambra is the palace and fortress complex of the Nasrid
    rulers. Fine geometric decoration, inscriptions, courtyards, and flowing water
    create a calm yet captivating atmosphere. Its Arabic name means Red Castle, a
    meaning made clear when the outer walls take on a warm colour at sunset.
  _sector: Granada / SPAIN
  _displayTitleTurkish: "El Hamra Saray\u0131"
  _shortDescriptionTurkish: "El Hamra, Nasr\xEE h\xFCk\xFCmdarlar\u0131n\u0131n saray
    ve kale kompleksidir. \u0130nce geometrik s\xFCslemeler, yaz\u0131lar, avlular
    ve akan suyun birlikte kullan\u0131m\u0131 yap\u0131ya sakin ama b\xFCy\xFCleyici
    bir atmosfer kazand\u0131r\u0131r. Ad\u0131 Arap\xE7ada \u201CK\u0131z\u0131l
    Kale\u201D anlam\u0131na gelir; g\xFCn bat\u0131m\u0131nda s\u0131cak bir renge
    b\xFCr\xFCnen d\u0131\u015F duvarlar\u0131 bu ismi hemen anla\u015F\u0131l\u0131r
    k\u0131lar."
  _sectorTurkish: "Granada / \u0130SPANYA"
